+def get_counterfactual_teacher_prompt() -> str:
+    """Generic verifier-grounded policy for a counterfactual rollout teacher."""
+    return dedent("""\
+        # Verifier-grounded counterfactual execution
+
+        Your trajectory is judged by the final environment state, not by whether
+        an individual tool call returns successfully. Before any mutation,
+        decompose the task into all requested state constraints and inspect the
+        relevant existing records with read, get, list, search, or check tools.
+        Do not create duplicate state when the requested state already exists.
+
+        When a mutation is needed, include every constraint explicitly requested
+        by the task. After the mutation, read the affected state again and verify
+        every requested field and relationship. A successful tool response alone
+        does not mean the task is complete. Produce a final answer only after the
+        resulting environment state has been checked against the full task.
+        Use one concrete environment tool action per turn.
+    """)
